---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const description =
  "Ecuadorist is an independent English-language guide to Ecuador for travelers, digital nomads, and retirees.";
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">The masthead</p>
    <h1>About Ecuadorist</h1>
    <p>
      Ecuadorist is an independent guide for English-speaking travelers, people who work remotely, and anyone considering a longer stay in Ecuador. The voice is a magazine’s: large photographs, short chapters, and no filler.
    </p>
    <h2>What we will and will not invent</h2>
    <p>
      Places named here are real. We do not invent prices, opening hours, phone numbers, or street addresses. Kitchens change hands and visa rules move. When a fact matters to a booking or a move, confirm it with the place itself or with an official source.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      Ecuadorist is not a law firm, a clinic, a bank, or a travel agency. The visa chapter is an overview, written so you know which door to open. It is not advice for your situation.
    </p>
    <h2>A note on the airport</h2>
    <p>
      Links to <a href="https://uiotransfers.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UIO Transfers</a> go to the site owner’s own airport-transfer company in Quito. Those links are not third-party advertisements. Other partner links are explained on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Photographs</h2>
    <p>
      Photography is drawn from Wikimedia Commons under licenses that allow this use. Every image is credited on the <a href="/credits/">credits</a> page, with the photographer and the license.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
